LOGBOOK.md:12:- BINDINGS: macOS-only generated graph; MTU/buffers/batching/HEV values 1500/32768/64/5ms/24576/4096/2/500 with no HEV fork; selected pinned libssh2/OpenSSL adapter with exact algorithm, window, rekey, lifecycle, notice, maintenance, and revalidation constraints. Deferred iOS, MTU 4096/8500, whole-extension memory, general UDP, lanes, reconnect, and M3 tuning remain blocked/deferred.
LOGBOOK.md:127:- GATES: Every M0 viability row maps evidence for both candidates. libssh2 has no waived red row; ReluxNIOSSH's missing neutral TCP ownership, opaque signer, bounded intake, algorithm reporting, keepalive, and unbuilt adapter rows remain explicit. The four deferred semantics remain unsupported/notReported under `TASK-260728-3cveay`; physical scale, extension memory, soak, and DNS footprint remain M3 gates.
LOGBOOK.md:130:- CONFIG GAP: Independent review found that positive-only rekey values did not satisfy the required range contract. The ADR now limits M0 composition to 4 KiB–5 GiB protected bytes, 100 ms–1 hour elapsed time, and the executed 10 s completion timeout. These are an admissible candidate envelope, not production defaults; `TASK-260715-1pn983` plus the M3 tuning/final matrix own final winners and any wider timeout range.
LOGBOOK.md:177:- VERIFICATION: The complete 26-test real-sshd libssh2 integration suite and full 428-test Swift suite pass, including server-side unapproved-key rejection, primary/fallback algorithms, host-policy ordering, channel rejection, M0 flows, and rekey-safe traffic. Thirty-three Python tests pass; live four-server lifecycle plus tests produce 83.7% line coverage for the fixture orchestrator and 88.3% for the provider. Integration tests prove real first-use/change/auth/channel failures, exact task-owned rotation, 128 KiB byte-exact transfer across a 32 KiB server rekey limit, endpoint behaviors, real latency/loss proxies, finite privacy-safe reports, and PID/state teardown. The full streamed 5 GiB source/sink reports exactly 5,368,709,120 bytes and `SHA256:fc01cfd7aebf90ff9491f8556131b6ef575c3e1fa33a0277ba28920bbaee7f54` without a payload file. Manifest/preflight validation, Python compilation/tab checks, strict Swift format lint, JSON parsing, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The live lifecycle reached Ubuntu 24.04/OpenSSH 9.6p1, macOS/OpenSSH 10.2p1 profiles, and the non-root real-host Darwin/OpenSSH 9.9p2 identity with public categorical output only.
LOGBOOK.md:187:- ROOT CAUSE: Reviewer round 3 passed the accepted cancellation, keepalive, and pressure regressions but unfiltered run 3 exposed a final fixture race in `rekeyCoalescingAndOpenScheduling`. The test intentionally held rekey while a first channel open consumed a real 300 ms deadline, then gave a second expected-success open the same real deadline. Aggregate scheduler latency could expire that second open before the observer resumed rekey, so a scheduler delay—not the production contract—selected `.timedOut`.
LOGBOOK.md:189:- VERIFICATION: The exact rekey/open case passes after the change, and the five cancellation/rekey/automatic-keepalive/channel-pressure regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A fresh reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and exit 0, including prior failure positions 3, 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, strict recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The pre/post sshd listener set remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815, and TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved algorithm matrix remains present.
LOGBOOK.md:205:- VERIFICATION: The exact scoped-cancellation/no-idle-timeout case passes 30/30 focused runs; the positive long-rekey keepalive case, the new fatal-keepalive regression, and all 25 LibSSH integration cases pass. Twenty consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs each pass 427 tests in 35 suites with exit 0, including the prior run-13 and run-16 failure points. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The before/after sshd listener set remains the same two older PIDs, 1330 and 34815; no validation-owned listener leaked. TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved-algorithm matrix remains intact.
LOGBOOK.md:220:- MATRIX: The real-loopback-sshd libssh2 gate passes 46 tests across adapter, bridge, and provider-contract suites. A new test-only compatibility row forces and verifies both approved transport sets: curve25519/Ed25519/aes256-ctr/hmac-sha2-256 and group14-sha256/P-256/aes128-ctr/hmac-sha2-512. Client byte/time/manual rekey, server-rekey-safe traffic, keepalive transmission, direct/exec/upload, bounded pressure, cancellation, privacy, and zero-owned-resource cleanup pass.
LOGBOOK.md:222:- VERIFICATION: libssh2 artifact/source/rekey gates, strict Swift format, four extension-safe macOS arm64/x86_64 adapter/harness builds, and affected tests exit 0. Affected adapter coverage is 80.28% regions / 93.86% functions / 90.04% lines.
LOGBOOK.md:230:- VERIFICATION: Golden taxonomy, hostile-text/prohibited-data, cancellation, NSError redaction, socket/URL, NWError, OSStatus, runtime-snapshot, selected libssh2 timeout, and live authentication-timeout tests pass. Recursive Swift format lint, boundary/native/libssh2 verification, all 425 Swift tests in 35 suites, `swift build`, and `git diff --check` exit 0.
