+# TASK-260715-3ejhyy — developer rework outcome
+
+## Result
+
+Ready for review. Revision-1 findings F1–F3 are resolved in the production call
+site and exact returned runtime graphs.
+
+## Accepted dependency pin
+
+- Sole source: `Configuration/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`
+- Spawned precondition: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`
+- Both copies: 17,492 bytes
+- Both copies SHA-256: `40333862b46b7af04cdd966ade91e8c9cc917e573c6601e26e7fa956d11ae161`
+- Production validation reports `productionCompositionPermitted=true`, no failures,
+  and the same manifest digest.
+
+## Rework delivered
+
+1. `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()` no longer accepts an
+   arbitrary `makeSSHBootstrap` closure. It constructs the selected libssh2
+   transport, system-domain Keychain credential resolver, immutable-snapshot
+   approved-host policy, and privacy-safe credential diagnostic mapper itself.
+   Public injections contain only candidate-neutral profile/configuration,
+   network, logging/metrics, TCP/DNS, and settings seams.
+2. The concrete candidate-neutral macOS SSH bootstrap loads and verifies the
+   immutable profile, validates the connection configuration against the runtime
+   snapshot and selected capabilities, composes host policy before credential
+   lookup, connects the transport, and returns an owned `M1SSHChannelSession`.
+   Concrete libssh2 types do not cross Core.
+3. Production packet preflight constructs only the resource-free
+   `M1HEVSOCKSConnectionAdapter` and bridge owner. The private listener,
+   descriptor, HEV lease/thread, and PacketFlow read are acquired only by the
+   post-settings `PacketBridge.start` path in `activateReads`.
+4. Exact macOS and deterministic harness smoke tests drive the runtime returned
+   by each factory through startup and two stop calls. They prove at-most-once
+   SSH/TCP/DNS/packet construction, zero packet ownership before settings,
+   post-settings activation, and reverse idempotent release.
+5. Manifest integer validation rejects CFBoolean, fractional, and overflowing
+   JSON numbers rather than coercing them through `NSNumber.intValue`.
+6. The existing Core boundary gate now rejects any reintroduced public
+   SSH-bootstrap/security override and requires all four root-owned mandatory
+   dependencies at `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()`.
+
+## Verification
+
+| Gate | Result | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Focused composition | exit 0; 9/9 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-test-composition-rework-02.log` |
+| Exact macOS production ownership | exit 0; 1/1 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-test-ownership-03.log` |
+| Exact deterministic harness ownership | exit 0; 3/3 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-test-harness-rework-02.log` |
+| Full SwiftPM suite | exit 0; 507 tests / 43 suites; 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-test-full-rework-01.log` |
+| Core target build | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-build-core-rework-01.log` |
+| macOS adapter target build | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-build-macos-adapter-rework-01.log` |
+| Harness-support target build | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-build-harness-support-rework-01.log` |
+| Unsigned macOS host/provider Debug+Release matrix | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/macos-targets-validate-rework-01.log` |
+| Core/security boundary guard | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/check-core-boundaries-rework-01.log` |
+| Accepted M0 validation | exit 0; permitted, no failures | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/m0-bindings-check-rework-01.log` |
+| M0 negative suite | exit 0; 32/32 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/m0-bindings-test-rework-01.log` |
+| Native/libssh2 pins and linkage | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/check-native-dependencies-rework-01.log` |
+| Strict recursive Swift format | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/swift-format-lint-rework-final.log` |
+| `git diff --check` | exit 0 | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/git-diff-check-rework-final.log` |
+| Board validation | process exit 0; one reported parent aggregate mismatch | `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/task-board-validate-rework-final.log` |
+
+## Negative evidence and production call site
+
+- `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()` refuses absent, unreadable,
+  digest-drifted, permission-disabled, superseded, pin-drifted,
+  capability-incomplete, and incompatible binding input before component
+  construction or routes.
+- `semanticIntegerTypes` narrows integer fields to booleans, fractions, and
+  overflow values and requires semantic refusal.
+- `exactGraphLifecycle` proves the composed host-policy and credential paths are
+  called, and that packet ownership events cannot occur before settings apply.
+- `scripts/check-core-boundaries.sh` rejects a narrowed public factory surface
+  that exposes `makeSSHBootstrap`, selected transport, credential provider,
+  host-policy factory, or diagnostic mapper overrides; it also requires the
+  mandatory calls to remain in the production entry point.
+- `dnsOnlyUDPDispatch` admits virtual-DNS TCP/UDP and requires ordinary UDP to
+  fail with `generalUDPDeferred`.
+
+## Preserved failures and anomalies
+
+- Rework compile attempts 01–03 exited 1 while the new Core/native imports,
+  UUID/string validation, and test factory API were being corrected. Logs are
+  retained under `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/`.
+- The first rework strict lint exited 1 on mechanical formatting and the final
+  recursive lint exits 0.
+- One attempted multi-item board checklist mutation exited 1 because task-board
+  permits one checklist activity per mutation. The five atomic mutations then
+  exited 0.
+- `task-board validate` returned process exit 0 while reporting the owning Story
+  stored as `to-dev` versus its child aggregate `development`. This parent state
+  is orchestrator-owned and is recorded as an issue, not described as clean.
+- No live Keychain lookup, SSH network connection, provider launch, VPN start,
+  route/DNS mutation, or PacketFlow/HEV runtime was performed by the deterministic
+  ownership tests. The provider matrix was build/validation only.
+
+## Review focus
+
+- `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime()` and its public component
+  factory surface for the eliminated SSH bypass.
+- `MacOSProductionSSHBootstrap` for immutable profile/security dependency order.
+- `M1HEVSOCKSConnectionAdapter`, `BridgeBackedM1PacketPlaneSession.activateReads`,
+  and the exact production/harness ownership tests for preflight and teardown.
